 ],
 "text": "Your AI assistant just spent $4,000 from your debit card. On a standing desk, three pairs of sneakers, and an online course on how to use AI. You never ask for any of it. It's 9am. Your bank app keeps buzzing, your coffee is going cold, and the assistant is asking if you'd like it to track the deliveries. What do you do first? Here's what the rules actually say. In the US, if you report an unauthorized debit card charge within two business days, the most you can lose is $50. Wait longer, and it can rise to $500. Every hour you spend arguing with the assistant is costing you. Wait more than 60 days after your statement, and you could lose all of it. The bank's answer becomes, sorry, that one's on you, so you get one move. Option A, call your bank right now and report it. Option B, ask the store for a refund first, and only call the bank if they refuse. Comment A or B. Part two shows what happens next."
}